[opheld1,wom_book_2]
    ~mesbox("The Myth of the Elder-dragons | Long before the gods came here, so the tale runs, a race of Elder-dragons walked this world.");

[opheld1,rd_chem_book]
    ~mesbox("Notes on reactions. Room temperature unless stated. | Cupric sulfate and dihydrogen monoxide: a blue compound, along with heat. Exothermic. | Gypsum and dihydrogen monoxide: a white, heat-resistant solid much like plaster. Exothermic. | Cupric ore powder and tin ore powder: they bond at a remarkably low temperature. Liquid bronze, formed quite easily. | Nitrous monoxide could not be tested, being a gas. | Most other pairings at room temperature: nothing of use.");

